# SwiftFormat config for the Apple clients. Format from apps/apple:
# `swiftformat .`; check without writing: `swiftformat --lint .`.
# CI enforces the lint check (see apple.yml).
#
# The tree uses 2-space indent (matching the repo's Biome style); the rest
# is SwiftFormat defaults, pinned here so a default change fails loudly in
# review instead of silently reformatting the tree.
--swift-version 6.2
--indent 2
--tabwidth 2
--semicolons never
--trailing-commas never
--self remove

# SwiftPM build output and fetched dependencies, when present locally.
--exclude Packages/*/.build

# Test function names are author-chosen symbols (`swift test --filter`
# workflows match on them); never rewrite them into sentences.
--disable swiftTestingTestCaseNames

# Multiline-statement braces stay on the same line: SwiftLint's
# `opening_brace` requires it (and so does the Kodeco guide), while
# SwiftFormat's wrapMultilineStatementBraces would force them onto their
# own line. The two tools cannot both pass — SwiftLint wins.
--disable wrapMultilineStatementBraces
